<!-- ══════════════════════════════ INSTALL ══════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="sec" id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div>
        <div class="sec-kicker">python {{PYFLOOR}}+, zero dependencies</div>
        <h2>Three routes. All of them run offline.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>No key, no account, no GPU. The proxy answers from a heuristic the first second
        you start it; the local checkpoint is an upgrade you opt into later.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="routes">
      <div class="route">
        <div class="route-n">install.sh</div>
        <h3>From source</h3>
        <p>The route the README's first code block uses. Builds a wheel and installs it into the active interpreter.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><span class="pfx">$</span><code id="cmd-git">git clone https://github.com/aashish254/limen &amp;&amp; cd limen &amp;&amp; ./install.sh</code><button data-copy="cmd-git">copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="route">
        <div class="route-n">pip install .</div>
        <h3>Into a clean venv</h3>
        <p>What CI does. Nothing on the machine is touched, which is the only honest way to try a tool.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><span class="pfx">$</span><code id="cmd-venv">python3 -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; source .venv/bin/activate &amp;&amp; pip install .</code><button data-copy="cmd-venv">copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="route">
        <div class="route-n">subproto demo</div>
        <h3>See it decide</h3>
        <p>Seventeen synthetic agent requests through the proxy, no upstream, no spend. Start here.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><span class="pfx">$</span><code id="cmd-demo">subproto demo --slots &amp;&amp; subproto report</code><button data-copy="cmd-demo">copy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="th-note" style="margin-top:22px">Then <b>subproto doctor</b> — it reads this
      machine and tells you what is present, what is optional, and what to install. It names key
      <i>variables</i> and never a key. Gated on <b>{{PYVERSIONS}}</b>; this run was
      <b>{{PYTHON}}</b> on a {{HOST}} at load {{LOAD}}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

